# Salesforce Sales-Team Skills — Ambient Grounding

This workspace ships three Cursor commands and three corresponding Claude
Code skills. They live under `.claude/skills/` (canonical) with `.cursor/`
shims that delegate to the same source files. The slash commands are:

- `/focus-group` — multi-persona, multi-model review panel for Salesforce
  sales conversations. Default product pack: Salesforce CRM + Agentforce.
  13 product packs + 19 industry packs + a `--generic` bypass. See
  [`.claude/skills/focus-group/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/focus-group/SKILL.md)
  and
  [`.claude/skills/focus-group/references/persona-roster.md`](.claude/skills/focus-group/references/persona-roster.md).

- `/download` — runtime-adaptive harvester for Salesforce help /
  Trailhead / Architect / developer.salesforce.com and any other URL.
  Saves citations under `references/<slug>/`. See
  [`.claude/skills/download/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/download/SKILL.md).

- `/cross-ai-review` — fans one prompt across whichever AI CLIs are
  installed (Claude, Codex, Gemini, opencode), with a multi-Claude
  fallback (Opus + Sonnet) when only Claude is present. See
  [`.claude/skills/cross-ai-review/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/cross-ai-review/SKILL.md).

- `/anonymize` — bidirectional placeholder anonymization for LLM-bound
  text. Scrub customer names, PII, financial figures into placeholders
  before sending to any external LLM; restore real values after the
  response comes back. Library called by the other three skills; also
  usable standalone. Aggressive-by-default. Local map never leaves the
  laptop. See
  [`.claude/skills/anonymize/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/anonymize/SKILL.md).

- `/slackbot` — build an anonymized customer profile from the user's
  Slack workspace via the Slack MCP (member-only scope, never DMs).
  Output runs through `/anonymize` before any persona prompt sees it.
  See
  [`.claude/skills/slackbot/SKILL.md`](.claude/skills/slackbot/SKILL.md).

## When to invoke each one

| User intent | Skill to invoke |
|-------------|-----------------|
| "Review my discovery questions for an Acme call" | `/focus-group` |
| "What would an SE / Champion / CIO say about this draft?" | `/focus-group` |
| "Pull the Salesforce docs on Service Cloud Voice" | `/download` |
| "Capture this customer's About page and IR materials" | `/download` |
| "Fact-check this proposal across two or three AIs" | `/cross-ai-review` |
| "Did I get any claims here wrong?" | `/cross-ai-review` |

These skills are **explicit-trigger**: invoke them when the user runs
the slash command or explicitly asks for the behavior. Do not
auto-activate them from adjacent conversation about reviews, feedback,
decks, or personas.

## Customer-grounding gate (load-bearing for /focus-group)

When `/focus-group` is invoked and the user's prompt does not name a
specific customer or include explicit cultural/scale signals, **stop
and ask** before doing any research. The two-question gate is
specified in
[`.claude/skills/focus-group/references/org-profile-schema.md`](.claude/skills/focus-group/references/org-profile-schema.md).
The skill never silently produces a generic answer to a question that
obviously concerns a real customer.

## Voice rule (applies everywhere)

Plain, professional, neutral. No slang. No labels for the reader
(`noob`, `newbie`, `non-technical`, `layperson`). No jokes at the
reader's expense. The skills read the same whether the user is a
brand-new AE or a 20-year architect — only the depth of explanation
flexes, never the tone.

## Errors

Apply the err-doctrine at
[`.claude/skills/focus-group/references/err-doctrine.md`](.claude/skills/focus-group/references/err-doctrine.md):
four-line shape — cause / what-was-done / next-steps / *"If you'd
like, paste the screen you see and I'll translate it."*
